From 0b644c226dd1388e0ff222462f07f8695d537071 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:49:15 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Add QVideoFrameFormat::stereoMode and fill it in the FFmpeg
 backend

A stereoscopic 3D video holds both views in every frame, side by side or top
and bottom, and says so in the stream: the frame packing arrangement SEI of
H.264 (D.2.26) and H.265 (D.2.16), or Matroska's StereoMode (RFC 9559,
5.1.4.1.28.3). FFmpeg reads both into the Stereo 3D side data of the decoded
frames. Nothing in Qt Multimedia passed it on, so a player built on it could
not tell a 3D video from a wide or a tall one.

Add StereoMode to QVideoFrameFormat, with the four packings Qt Multimedia can
hand over (side by side and top and bottom, either eye first) and None for
everything else. The FFmpeg backend sets it from the frame's side data, as it
does for the mastering display's luminance. The SEI is sent with keyframes only
and holds until another replaces it (H.264 D.2.26, repetition period 1), so the
video renderer keeps the last packing it saw.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet via Claude Code
